WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.834
We're hanging out with
Billy Crystal right now.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.734
Now, Billy, you have
so many great bits

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.968
in all the comedy shows
you've done through the years.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:14.434
But my favorite bit is this one
bit that you do where you take

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:17.667
famous movie posters and you cut
out the mouths of the people

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:20.133
and then --
-You put the lips through.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:22.234
It's like you do impressions

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:23.767
without having to do
an impression.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:26.234
-Yeah.
-It's just the mouth.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.634
-The reason why I thought about
it is because today

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:29.868
we recently saw each other

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.501
as we were getting
our COVID test here at NBC.

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.200
And I remember it so clearly.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.200
-Yeah, it was earlier today.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.801
-Go ahead and take a seat.
We'll call you shortly.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.267
-Great, thanks.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.300
-Hey!
-Billy.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.834
Great to see you.
-How you doing?

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:51.434
Long time.
-Yeah.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.000
You're already dressed
for the show.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.434
-Yeah.
-Yeah, me too.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:57.334
I'm also miked for the show
as well.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.400
What do you think? No masks?
-No masks.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.968
That's good because I actually
got tired of my breath

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.467
smelling like I ate cat food.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:04.834
-Yeah, I hear you.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.133
Did you get your booster yet?

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.100
-Booster? Um...

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.501
Actually, I don't know,
you know.

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.934
I don't know.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:18.901
I got -- I got my booster,
you know,

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.767
on the day of
my daughter's wedding.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.434
-Oh, my God.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.834
Oh, no, no.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:30.934
Oh, oh, no way, man.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:34.300
Oh, no, no!

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.934
That is so cool, Marlon Brando.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.334
No way.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:42.167
-You know,
you don't have to do that.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.000
You're very pretty.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.801
-Oh, no, I can't believe
you said that I'm pretty.

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.067
Why would you do that?

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:52.868
-Listen, if you would talk
that fast,

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.801
I would have been able to
watch all of "Dune."

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.834
-Listen here.

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:08.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:11.767
Listen here, Mac.
Listen here, Mac.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.000
You think gas is a problem now.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.567
We used to have to fill our cars
up back in my day with steam.

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.033
They were all steam engines.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:23.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.267
I remember Mom --
Mom used to say --

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:28.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:29.868
Mom used to say all the time --

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:36.000
would say, "Joey, Joey, don't
spend hours hocking loogies

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.033
into the side of the truck."

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:42.734
Head over to the sock hop
to get root beer salad.

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:45.067
-Yeah, yeah, salad.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.801
Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.267
I like, you know, yeah.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:50.934
Yeah, salad.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:54.968
I got -- I got twins, twins.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:58.701
I got to buy two salads
for the twins, you know?

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.334
Two Caesar salads.

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:05.934
I got a Cesar Romero salad
and a Julio Cesar Chavez salad.

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:09.167
[ Laughter ]
And yeah, yeah, it's wild.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.501
Twins, yeah.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:15.801
-Okay, gang, okay, gang, gang,
I don't think that's allowed.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.868
Okay, okay, that's -- Guys, we
can't do that, okay, gang?

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:21.267
Okay, guys, guys, guys,
we can't do that.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.701
Alright? We can't do that.

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.467
-Are you telling me
that I can't do that?

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.267
Are you telling me
that I can't do that?

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.467
I don't think you want to tell
me that I can't do that.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:36.534
Yeah. No Nobu for you.
No Nobu for you.

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.033
-I can't believe --
I can't believe you own Nobu.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:40.367
That's like the craziest --

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:44.167
You know, 'cause I love sushi
and I didn't even know --

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.234
I took Sandy to the beach,
you know.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:50.100
We get like -- catch a fish
and go get some sushi, right?

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:53.868
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:58.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:00.434
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:04.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:07.300
-Mr. Crystal?
They're ready for your tests.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.267
-Oh. Thank you.
-Mult-- Tests?

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:11.367
Multiple tests?

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:13.334
-Yeah, I'm also getting
a colonoscopy.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.167
It was a two-for-one sale.

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:19.133
And actually...

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:20.868
It was an offer
I couldn't refuse.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:23.734
-Absolutely,
why would you do that?

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.367
You don't have to do it.

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:27.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.901
I love you, buddy.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.400
That was so great.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.801
That's Billy Crystal
right there. Come on.

